.TH HTTP_BODY 3
.SH NAME
http_body \- set the body of the request
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <http.h>
.P
.BI "int http_body(http* " h ", const char* " x ", size_t " n ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION

.BR http_body ()
appends n bytes to the body of the request that was started last. It is sent with a Content-Length. Not possible after http_chunked(3).
.SH RETURN VALUE
1 on success, 0 on failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
http_chunk(3)
